#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# position_smallest

#% text
# `position_smallest(xs)` gives the positions of the smallest elements of `xs` in numerical order.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Every position with the smallest value is given, each as a list `[i]`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
position_smallest([3, 1, 2])
#% output
#= [[2]]

#% cell
position_smallest([1, 3, 1])
#% output
#= [[1], [3]]

#% cell
position_smallest([pi, e, 3])
#% output
#= position_smallest([pi, e, 3])

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
position_smallest([-1.5, -0.5, -2])
#% output
#= [[3]]

#% cell
position_smallest([])
#% output
#= []

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `position_largest`, `min`, `ordering`, `take_smallest`
